\label{rmk5}{\rm 
Note that item (iv) in Corollary \ref{cor4} cannot be applied to the case of $r$-plateaued functions, where $r>0$. We write $W_{f}(x)=(-1)^{g(x)}2^{\frac{m+r}{2}}1_{S_{f}}(x)$ for $g \in \mathcal{BF}_{m}$. By  \cite[Theorem 5]{WH}, the minimum weight codewords of $\mathcal{C}_{\mathbb{AD}_f}$ are $(g(b)+b \cdot p+f(p))_{p \in \mathbb{F}_{2}^{m}}$, where $b \in S_{f}$. Let $f'_{b}(p)=g(b)+b \cdot p+f(p)$, where $b \in S_{f}$ and $p \in \mathbb{F}_{2}^{m}$. Thus the support of the minimum weight codeword $(g(b)+b \cdot p+f(p))_{p \in \mathbb{F}_{2}^{m}}$ is $\{p \in \mathbb{F}_{2}^{m}: f'_{b}(p)=1\}$. By Corollary \ref{cor3.2}, if the minimum weight codewords support a design, then for any distinct $p, q \in \mathbb{F}_{2}^{m}$, $\sum_{b \in S_{f}}(-1)^{f'_{b}(p)+f'_{b}(q)}$ should be a constant. However, $\sum_{b \in S_{f}}(-1)^{f'_{b}(p)+f'_{b}(q)}=(-1)^{f(p)+f(q)}\sum_{b \in S_{f}}(-1)^{(p+q) \cdot b}$, which is not a constant in general.                                                                                                                                                          
